    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the **Austin Waves** is anchored by the explosive matchup profile of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who stands as our premier start. Facing a porous 5.20 xERA from the opposing arm, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from both a favorable park and wind conditions, with his batting order spot (#1) and dynamic platoon advantage elevating him well into elite territory. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (76.93) and **Andy Pages** (72.90) offer strong returns against Jeffrey Springs; their scores are bolstered by park factors and a high-leverage opportunity to exploit an SP with a 4.46 xERA. **Miguel Vargas** (66.77) also warrants attention, as his strong xwOBA profile and high-order placement make him a vital component of our offense today.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Nolan Schanuel** (42.30), who narrowly missed the cut for the final utility spot. While his base projections were respectable, the presence of Bryan Woo on the mound created too much friction, depressing his score through a -13% SP skill adjustment and a park penalty that ultimately favored the higher-ceiling versatility of **Josh Jung** (55.09). We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Lowe**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill** closely; as these remain \"Lineup Pending,\" any late-scratch or order drop could significantly impact their utility. Specifically, we are exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** (47.22), as he faces a tough matchup against Matthew Boyd and ranks as a marginal start, saved only by the necessity of depth in a 5x5 Roto grind. We will look for **Nasim Nunez** (48.21) to provide modest value on the basepaths, as his slow-delivering opponent provides a distinct opportunity to chase the scarcest category in our format: Stolen Bases.",
